There's no particular reason that each player's
scavenger list be the same as one for another player
or one for another game by the current player, just
make the list for each game a subset of length N of
a much larger list, and make each player's list (for
each separate game) be some subset (of equal length)
of that larger list.

I like your idea of spreading the list as floor
engravings, all around the dungeon too, which forces
the player to stomp every grid cell in the dungeon
(inherently dangerous because of traps) to learn the
list, and especially if the engravings are as rubbed
almost unreadable as is currently the case for the
existing engravings.

